PC REASSEMBLY STEPS
===================

1. INSTALL THE MOTHERBOARD
---------------------------
I placed the motherboard back into the PC case and aligned it with the
standoffs and rear ports. I tightened the screws carefully so the
motherboard stayed firmly in place.

2. INSTALL THE POWER SUPPLY
---------------------------
I placed the power supply into its position and secured it with screws.
Installing it before connecting the main cables makes it easier to route
the cables properly.

3. INSTALL THE CPU COOLER
-------------------------
I placed the CPU cooler back on the CPU and connected its fan cable to
the motherboard. The cooler must be installed correctly because it keeps
the CPU at a safe temperature.

4. INSTALL THE RAM
------------------
I inserted the RAM modules into the correct motherboard slots until the
clips locked into place. RAM needs to be installed properly so the PC
can start and use system memory.

5. INSTALL THE HDD/SSD
----------------------
I placed the storage drive back into its bay or M.2 slot and secured it.
I connected the required SATA data and power cables for the drive.

6. INSTALL THE GPU
------------------
I inserted the graphics card into the PCIe slot and secured it with the
case screw. I also connected its power cable if required. The GPU must
be firmly installed for proper display and graphics performance.

7. CONNECT THE CABLES
---------------------
I reconnected the motherboard power cable, CPU power cable, storage
cables, front-panel cables, fan cables, and GPU power cable. Connecting
the cables carefully prevents loose connections and ensures all
components receive power.

8. CHECK ALL CONNECTIONS
------------------------
I checked that every component and cable was properly connected before
closing the case. This step is important because finding a loose
connection is easier before the PC is fully closed.

9. REPLACE THE SIDE PANEL
-------------------------
I placed the side panel back onto the case and tightened the screws.
The panel protects the internal components and keeps the case properly
enclosed.

10. RECONNECT POWER AND TEST THE PC
-----------------------------------
I connected the power cable, switched on the power supply, and started
the PC. I checked that the fans, display, and other components were
working normally.

WHY THE ORDER MATTERS
=====================
The order is important because some components and cables are easier to
install before other parts block access to them. Installing the
motherboard, cooler, RAM, storage, and GPU in a logical order also
reduces the chance of damaging components or forgetting a connection.
